{"name":"Warm Embrace","hex":"#93817e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"warm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a somewhat high temperature, often but not always connoting that the high temperature is pleasant rather than uncomfortable.","Friendly and with affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make or keep warm.","To become warm, to heat up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warm"},{"term":"embrace","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To clasp (someone or each other) in the arms with affection; to take in the arms; to hug.","To seize (something) eagerly or with alacrity; to accept or take up with cordiality; to welcome."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of putting arms around someone and bringing the person close to the chest; a hug.","An enclosure partially or fully surrounding someone or something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embrace"}],"entries":[{"title":"Breezy (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Breezy is the tenth studio album by the American singer Chris Brown, released on June 24, 2022, as the follow-up to his 2019 album Indigo. The artists featured on the album are Lil Wayne, Anderson .Paak, Blxst, Lil Baby, H.E.R., EST Gee, Wizkid, Jack Harlow, Tory Lanez, Fivio Foreign, Ella Mai, Yung Bleu, Capella Grey, Lil Durk, Davido, and Bryson Tiller."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Chris_Brown_-_Breezy.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breezy_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/The_Breezy_sign.jpg/500px-The_Breezy_sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/The_Breezy_sign.jpg/500px-The_Breezy_sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A fan holding up a si